    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling performance today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.89). **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive +16% park factor adjustment and a favorable matchup against Luinder Avila. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages a strong dynamic platoon edge against the lefty JP Sears, solidifying his spot as a core building block. In the outfield, **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Kyle Tucker** (73.09) provide excellent efficiency; **Jackson Merrill** is particularly well-positioned, utilizing a +13% platoon advantage against Shane Bieber, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a high-floor start despite a challenging matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Jung**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 53.34. While his matchup against Hunter Brown is manageable, the optimizer favored the higher overall output of **Dominic Smith** (53.61) and **Sam Antonacci** (53.60), who benefited slightly more from their respective situational metrics and projected batting order slots. It was a marginal call, but we are prioritizing the volume from our active utility spots. We are also keeping a close eye on **Jorge Polanco** on the bench; despite his decent projection, a 38% rain risk against Sonny Gray made him an easy exclusion for today\u2019s card.\n\nFinally, owners should monitor the official lineup releases as all current scores are based on projected batting positions. **Josh Lowe** (66.88) and **Andy Pages** (72.83) carry significant upside due to their respective stolen base potential against slow-delivery pitchers, making them high-leverage assets in our chase for category scarcity. While **Drake Baldwin** (59.40) and **Miguel Vargas** (63.96) offer solid contributions, ensure that **Miguel Vargas**\u2014who boasts an elite 0.402 xwOBA\u2014retains his anticipated spot in the order to fully realize his statistical potential against Jacob Lopez.",
